    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. specifically with the infection part, what are the biggest red flags that indicate things are going south internally? like if i can't see anything wrong on the skin yet, what should i be watching for in her behavior or general state?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Monitor the heifer's behavior and physical condition for signs of internal complications, such as lethargy, decreased appetite, water avoidance, or decreased mammary excretion. Also, look for labored breathing, swelling of the abdomen, or pain-related behaviors like kicking or backing. Additionally, keep an eye on the heifer's temperature, as a persistence of elevated temperature above 39.5°C (103.1°F) or a sudden spike may indicate internal infection.",
