      "content": "You can start supplementing with a strong, high-quality hay or concentrate, typically containing 12-15% crude protein and 40-60% fiber, to support the return of ruminal fermentation. This can help jumpstart the fermentation process and provide the necessary nutrients for the heifer's continued recovery. However, always consult with a veterinarian before introducing any supplements, and avoid feeding too many feedstuffs too quickly, as this can lead to ruminal acidosis.",
